/*
 * MPU6050 accelerometer sampler for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B.
 *
 * Samples acceleration data at 100 Hz using a POSIX per-process timer
 * (SIGEV_SIGNAL) and stores the most recent sample in a circular buffer.
 *
 * Build:  gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o mpu6050_accel mpu6050_accel.c
 *
 * The driver library interface is a simple sysfs-style interface that
 * exposes the most recent X/Y/Z acceleration values as read-only files:
 *
 *   /sys/kernel/mpu6050_accel/latest/x
 *   /sys/kernel/mpu6050_accel/latest/y
 *   /sys/kernel/mpu6050_accel/latest/z
 *
 * The driver is created and removed by the kernel module
 * mpu6050_accel_drv.c.  The module is compiled into the kernel and
 * loaded/unloaded by the build script.
 */

